{"task_id": "ab8df6491b4c8af0", "model_key": "zai-glm-5-3-flash", "raw_response": "2^1000002 ≡ 1 (mod 1000003, prime), so 2^(10^10) = 2^(10^10 mod 1000002). Since 10^10 = 10^4·10^6 and 10^6 ≡ −2 (mod 1000002), exponent ≡ −20000 ≡ 980002, and 2^980002 = 2^(−20000).\n\nComputing 2^20000 mod 1000003 by binary exponentiation (20000 = 16384+2048+1024+512+32) gives 2^20000 ≡ 941029. Extended Euclid: 197510·941029 − 185863·1000003 = 1, so 941029⁻¹ ≡ 197510.\n\n{\"answer\": \"197510\"}", "parsed_answer": "197510", "correct": false, "parse_status": "wrong", "error": null, "latency_ms": 69542, "usage": {"input": 292, "output": 5611, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 0, "totalTokens": 5903, "cost": {"input": 4.38e-05, "output": 0.0028055, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0028493}}, "cost_usd": 0.0028493, "attempts": 1, "model_info": {"provider": "opencode-go", "model": "glm-5.3-flash", "api": "openai-completions", "thinkingLevel": "low", "responseId": "053f985c-5b1c-4270-90bd-bb33ccb03fbb"}, "stop_reason": "stop", "started_at": "2026-10-17T15:41:01+00:00", "finished_at": "2026-10-17T15:42:10+00:00"}
